  - Q1/Q2 2D: 98/112 configurations qualified. LSPG-CN-R 2Δt₀ fails Q1 for R128 and R256 at every mesh (val32|19: 3.6–4.0e-4 > 2.5e-4). R128 CN-R 2.5Δt₀ fails Q2 marginally (~2.50e-4); fallback fib6765 passes Q2 but fails Q1. 256² R384 CN-R 2.5Δt₀ fails Q2; its gauss160 fallback qualifies. Reproduction gates vs combined: 21 × 38 cases, worst 1.8e-15.
  - B5 fronts: GAL-CN (registered diagnostic) holds 6/7 median-front places at every mesh; most accurate R384 GAL-CN Δt₀ 0.050 % median at 1.31× reference cost (1.5× at 4096²). Worst-error front shared by LSPG-CN-R and LSPG-BE.
  - B4 order: LSPG-BE 1; GAL-CN 2; LSPG-CN-R 2 at R384 (p̂ 1.96), 1.74 at R128 (no integer label); over Δt₀..Δt₀/4.
  - B1: H-acc-N 21 pass / 9 inconclusive (5 unqualified; 4 GAL-CN small-error cases over the 10 % margin at 256²). H-acc-r: 128–512 "not monotone" in 20 cells, 7 inconclusive; 128–384: 14 monotone, 3 not monotone, 10 inconclusive (extended scheme/Δt set; P1's 6 primary cells were all monotone).
  - 3D Q2: 4/55 tested speed3d configurations pass (W256 gl24 FS CN Δt 0.01 and 0.0125; W256 lat8192 QN BDF2 0.025; W512 lat16384 QN BDF2 0.025). Round limit reached with 16 candidates exposed → "qualified subset of tested candidates", not a complete front.
